{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #293: declared status 'open'. Formalized: no. Let $k\\geq 1$ and let $v(k)$ be the minimal integer which does not appear as some $n_i$ in a solution to\\[1=\\frac{1}{n_1}+\\cdots+\\frac{1}{n_k}\\]with $1\\leq n_1<\\cdots <n_k$. Estimate the growth of $v(k)$. Current best: An elementary inductive argument shows that $n_k\\leq ku_k$ where $u_1=1$ and $u_{i+1}=u_i(u_i+1)$, and hence\\[v(k) \\leq kc_0^{2^k},\\]where\\[c_0=\\lim_n u_n^{1/2^n}=1.26408\\cdots\\]is the 'Vardi constant' (small improvements on this are possible as in [148]). Prize: no. Tags: number theory, unit fractions."},"claim_id":"vcl_c2e4aa70ba0e68371fac4bd4e1e3955d1de37adb30bac9b97681c92220ee4cee","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:293","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_0cb0543b7c087c45","object_root":"sha256:3f8dff306fb51f0e37c1ba69140af860c1b8de43263d86d9460c27c95f654328","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record","title":"erdos_d